                <pb facs="0056" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10113: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-19T20:00:00+01:00">April 19, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 20—10:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. My 337, April 19, 6 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d38-f1"/> The failure of the
                    Foreign Minister to clearly define his Government’s policy as set forth in my
                    telegram under reference, the tenor of recent editorial comment as previously
                    reported, the repercussion of news from Greece, and the apparently general
                    opinion of my American colleagues, gained by a canvass, that important decisions
                    concerning Spanish-Axis relations will be shortly made and acted upon by this
                    Government, make me feel that it would be highly desirable that the various
                    American Republics represented here (within the limits of their declared
                    policies in the present struggle against aggression) make their views known to
                    the Spanish Government especially to the end that its neutrality be maintained.
                    And this at the earliest moment.</p>
                <p>A military collapse in Greece or even a stalemate there would be controlling and
                    hastening factors designed for German-Spanish cooperation and action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
